\section{ADM Foliation and Tensor Definitions}

Let $(M, g_{\mu\nu})$ be a smooth, globally hyperbolic spacetime manifold
admitting a foliation into spacelike hypersurfaces $\Sigma_t$.
The ADM line element is
\[
ds^2 = -\alpha^2 dt^2 + \gamma_{ij}
(dx^i + \beta^i dt)(dx^j + \beta^j dt),
\]
where $\alpha$ is the lapse, $\beta^i$ the shift, and $\gamma_{ij}$ the
induced 3-metric.

The extrinsic curvature is defined by
\[
K_{ij} = -\frac{1}{2\alpha}
\left(\partial_t \gamma_{ij}
- \mathcal{D}_i \beta_j
- \mathcal{D}_j \beta_i\right),
\]
with $\mathcal{D}_i$ the covariant derivative compatible with
$\gamma_{ij}$.

